{"step_index":2008,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T17:41:42Z","content":"### ✅ Surge Route Handler & Deployment Restored\n\nThe \"project not found\" error on Surge happens when edge servers receive requests without an SPA catch-all fallback file (`200.html`).\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ What Was Fixed:\n1. **Added `200.html` SPA Catch-All:** Created `dist/200.html` mirroring `index.html` so Surge edge routing resolves all paths, sub-routes, and page refreshes cleanly.\n2. **Re-Published to Surge:** Deployed the complete bundle with PWA manifests, service worker, and dynamic Gemini model discovery.\n3. **Live Verified:** Verified HTTP `200 OK` response directly from **[`https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**.\n\n---\n\n### 🌐 Live Production Link\n👉 **[https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh](https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh)**\n\n*(If you see a cached error page in your browser, perform a quick hard refresh: `Ctrl + Shift + R` on Windows/Chrome, or `Cmd + Shift + R` / clear cache on Safari).*"}
