{"step_index":2014,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T21:22:21Z","thinking":"**Reviewing Recommended Enhancements**\n\nI'm currently reviewing the WORLD-CLASS ENHANCEMENT ROADMAP and the hybrid scheduling/calendar integration. Right now I am looking over the items listed in the \"Hybrid Calendar Scheduling & Piping\" section. The focus is to ensure a comprehensive integration and implementation strategy.\n\n\n**Implementing Calendar Integration**\n\nI've been working on integrating calendar features. I'm focusing on `.ics` generation for one-tap downloads, with Apple Calendar triggers for iOS and Mac. I'm also including direct web composer links for Google Calendar and Outlook/Office 365, with pre-filled event summaries. This functionality will be integrated into the appointment setting flow within the `DialerHudScreen` and `LeadDetailScreen`.\n\n\n**Developing Agent Dialing Tools**\n\nI'm developing features for agents, adding a school campus filter to the lead list so agents can dial educators at a single campus. I've integrated school filter support into the lead repository. Next I'll work on the planning period visual heatmap and weekly sit-down planner. This heatmap will show booked slots and allow 1-tap bookings. I'm also planning the interactive objection battlecards overlay in the HUD.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan for World-Class Enhancements: Hybrid Calendar Piping (Apple/Google/Outlook), Campus-Clustered Dialing, Planning Period Heatmap, Live Objection Battlecards, CSV Pipeline Sync, and Callback Reminders.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Implementation Plan: World-Class ValuTeachers Dialer & Calendar Suite\n\nThis plan details the implementation of the World-Class Enhancement Roadmap and the Hybrid Calendar Integration suite for SnapDialer.\n\n---\n\n## User Review Required\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - **Calendar Integration:** Provides 1-tap Apple Calendar (`.ics`), Google Calendar, and Outlook/Office 365 scheduling with pre-filled room numbers, planning periods, and 15-minute pre-bell alarms without requiring third-party API credentials.\n> - **Campus Batching:** Enables reps visiting a specific school to filter their calling queue down to that campus with a single tap.\n> - **Zero-Loss Guarantee:** All exports and CSV pipelines operate on top of the persistent IndexedDB engine.\n\n---\n\n## Proposed Architecture & Changes\n\n```\n                     ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                     │          SNAPDIALER WORLD-CLASS SUITE                  │\n                     └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘\n                                                │\n       ┌──────────────────┬─────────────────────┼────────────────────┬──────────────────┐\n       ▼                  ▼                     ▼                    ▼                  ▼\n[CALENDAR ENGINE]  [CAMPUS BATCHING]    [OBJECTION HUD]      [CSV SYNC]        [PLANNING HEATMAP]\n• Apple (.ics)     • Campus Clusters    • Live Battlecards   • Export CSV      • Mon-Fri Grid\n• Google Link      • School Queueing    • 1-Tap Scripts      • Roster Import   • Period 1-7 Slots\n• Outlook Link     • Proximity Sort     • FRS Objections     • Excel Format    • Double-Book Guard\n```\n\n---\n\n## Component Breakdown\n\n### 1. Hybrid Calendar Integration (`src/services/calendarService.ts`)\n- **RFC 5545 `.ics` Generator:** Generates downloadable and browser-launchable calendar events compatible with Apple Calendar (iOS/Mac) and Outlook.\n- **Google Calendar URL Builder:** Deep-links to Google Calendar template composer with start/end time, school location, and FRS notes.\n- **Outlook Web URL Builder:** Deep-links to Office 365 / Outlook Web composer.\n- **Auto-Alarm:** Injects a 15-minute pre-event notification reminder.\n\n### 2. Live Objection Battlecards HUD (`src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx` & `src/data/objections.ts`)\n- Interactive slide-over / modal drawer in the dialer HUD.\n- Battlecard categories for Florida teachers:\n  - *\"Already Have an Advisor\"*\n  - *\"Too Busy / No Time\"*\n  - *\"Only in Years 1–5\"*\n  - *\"What is DROP?\"*\n  - *\"Are You With the District / Union?\"*\n  - *\"Send Me Information via Email\"*\n- 1-tap to expand verbatim word-for-word talk tracks.\n\n### 3. Campus Clustered Geodialing (`src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`, `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`, `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`)\n- Dynamic School Campus selector chip strip (`All Schools`, `DeLand High (4)`, `Pine Ridge (3)`, etc.).\n- Launch Power Dialer filtered directly to a single campus.\n\n### 4. Planning Period Visual Heatmap (`src/screens/PlanningHeatmapScreen.tsx`)\n- Weekly schedule grid (Monday–Friday) across Florida school planning periods (Period 1 to Period 7 + After School).\n- Visual blocks showing confirmed sit-downs, pending requests, and open slots.\n- 1-tap to schedule directly from the grid.\n\n### 5. Two-Way CSV / Excel Pipeline Sync (`src/services/csvService.ts`)\n- **Export Pipeline:** Exports all leads and appointments with columns formatted for Excel / Google Sheets (`Name`, `Phone`, `School`, `Room #`, `Period`, `FRS Years`, `Status`, `Call Date`, `Notes`).\n- **Import Roster:** Bulk-upload CSV rosters with automatic column matching for Name, Phone, School, and Room.\n\n---\n\n## Verification Plan\n\n### Automated & Build Checks\n- `npx expo export -p web` to verify complete bundle compilation.\n- Type checks across all new services and screens.\n\n### Manual Verification\n- Test `.ics` file generation and Google Calendar link generation.\n- Test school campus filtering and queue launch.\n- Test objection battlecard popover in the HUD.\n- Test CSV export file download and CSV import parser.\n- Deploy to Surge (`https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`) and verify live operation.\n","Description":"Create implementation plan for World-Class Enhancements and Hybrid Calendar Suite","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3\\implementation_plan.md","toolAction":"Writing implementation plan","toolSummary":"Create implementation_plan.md"}}]}
